lingmo-clock (1.0.14+lingmo5u1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Add field labels, section headings and empty states to alarm, stopwatch and timer pages.
  * Install generated locale files with the Debian package.
  * Stage CMake install files in debian/tmp before dh_install distributes them.
  * Remove application build toolchains from the upload-only workflow.
  * Keep upload.yml focused on Debian source preparation and OBS upload.
  * Validate the Debian version suffix and base version in upload.yml.
  * Improve page hierarchy with descriptions, clearer alarm guidance and bounded timer inputs.
  * Prevent adding duplicate world-clock time zones.
  * Align the Clock title with the sidebar inset and update item text colors immediately on selection.
  * Use the installed clock theme glyph for the world clock sidebar entry.
  * Restore themed navigation icons in the SDK sidebar entries.
  * Use the shared SDK sidebar controls for application navigation.
  * Refine page hierarchy and group city, alarm and timer inputs into compact rows.
  * Add IANA city search, analog world clocks, alarm recurrence and snooze.
  * Preserve alarm service across UI exit and system/time-zone changes.
  * Add native stopwatch, circular countdown progress and timer sounds.

 -- Lingmo OS Team <team@lingmo.org>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0800

